1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,700
This is the whole first session.

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:04,960
Install it, set it up on

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:05,740
a real repo,

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,070
run something,

5
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:08,190
read the board.

6
00:00:08,417 --> 00:00:11,157
One idea to hold on to.

7
00:00:12,017 --> 00:00:13,457
Tyran is a manager for a

8
00:00:13,457 --> 00:00:14,097
team of agents.

9
00:00:14,997 --> 00:00:16,057
You stay the stakeholder.

10
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:19,826
Install is two slash commands inside

11
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:20,466
Claude Code.

12
00:00:21,026 --> 00:00:21,786
Then restart.

13
00:00:22,646 --> 00:00:24,166
Hooks and agents load at session

14
00:00:24,166 --> 00:00:24,679
start.

15
00:00:24,709 --> 00:00:27,929
Slash tyrant hello is the smoke

16
00:00:27,929 --> 00:00:28,339
test.

17
00:00:28,369 --> 00:00:30,209
If it answers, you are running.

18
00:00:30,829 --> 00:00:32,869
The only requirement is Claude Code

19
00:00:32,869 --> 00:00:33,769
two point one.

20
00:00:34,312 --> 00:00:37,092
Speak clearly at a natural pace

21
00:00:37,632 --> 00:00:39,612
with quiet confidence and a little

22
00:00:39,612 --> 00:00:40,212
warmth

23
00:00:41,292 --> 00:00:42,372
Slash tyrant setup,

24
00:00:43,052 --> 00:00:43,872
once per repository.

25
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:46,212
It reads how the repo is

26
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:46,952
really worked.

27
00:00:47,512 --> 00:00:48,732
Not how a the docs describes

28
00:00:48,732 --> 00:00:49,011
it.

29
00:00:49,041 --> 00:00:51,921
Every value it infers carries the

30
00:00:51,921 --> 00:00:53,101
fact that produced it.

31
00:00:53,681 --> 00:00:55,521
And it never grants itself the

32
00:00:55,521 --> 00:00:56,641
right to merge to main.

33
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:59,739
Then commit the dot tyran folder.

34
00:01:00,879 --> 00:01:02,879
Agents work in git worktrees, and

35
00:01:02,879 --> 00:01:05,179
a worktree carries no untracked files.

36
00:01:05,728 --> 00:01:08,348
Type slash tyran and describe the

37
00:01:08,348 --> 00:01:08,618
work.

38
00:01:08,648 --> 00:01:10,548
He interviews you first.

39
00:01:10,948 --> 00:01:12,208
At most four questions.

40
00:01:12,477 --> 00:01:14,697
After you accept the plan, the

41
00:01:14,697 --> 00:01:15,577
questions stop.

42
00:01:16,617 --> 00:01:18,717
Shall I continue is forbidden in

43
00:01:18,717 --> 00:01:19,977
the conductor's own file.

44
00:01:20,445 --> 00:01:22,165
Then the team goes out.

45
00:01:22,685 --> 00:01:24,605
A scout reads the repo first.

46
00:01:25,405 --> 00:01:26,805
Cheap tier, read only,

47
00:01:27,505 --> 00:01:28,055
fresh context.

48
00:01:28,327 --> 00:01:31,127
Implementers take one story each, on

49
00:01:31,127 --> 00:01:31,887
their own branch.

50
00:01:32,487 --> 00:01:34,167
Every one starts with an empty

51
00:01:34,167 --> 00:01:34,787
scrollback.

52
00:01:35,134 --> 00:01:37,554
The reviewer has no editing tools

53
00:01:37,554 --> 00:01:38,114
at all.

54
00:01:38,794 --> 00:01:40,234
A reviewer who can fix what

55
00:01:40,234 --> 00:01:42,494
they found approves their own patch.

56
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:44,280
Open the board.

57
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:46,880
One command, and this is the

58
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,940
one place a Node version matters.

59
00:01:49,314 --> 00:01:51,454
Overview answers one question.

60
00:01:52,134 --> 00:01:53,194
Is anything on fire.

61
00:01:54,274 --> 00:01:55,894
Two waiting on you.

62
00:01:56,694 --> 00:01:57,634
Five agents running.

63
00:01:58,694 --> 00:02:00,014
Forty seven percent merged.

64
00:02:00,505 --> 00:02:02,725
The Board tab is every ticket,

65
00:02:03,065 --> 00:02:05,065
in exactly one of ten lanes.

66
00:02:06,005 --> 00:02:07,965
Moving a ticket means appending an

67
00:02:07,965 --> 00:02:08,515
event.

68
00:02:08,786 --> 00:02:11,246
Say something halfway through and it

69
00:02:11,246 --> 00:02:13,146
does not land in the scrollback.

70
00:02:13,726 --> 00:02:14,906
It becomes a ticket.

71
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:16,926
Queued as T nine.

72
00:02:17,127 --> 00:02:19,307
The queue carries its open count

73
00:02:19,307 --> 00:02:20,287
in the tab label.

74
00:02:20,987 --> 00:02:22,827
A question you cannot see is

75
00:02:22,827 --> 00:02:24,167
a question you do not answer.

76
00:02:24,498 --> 00:02:26,678
Each card says whether a default

77
00:02:26,678 --> 00:02:27,458
is recorded.

78
00:02:28,538 --> 00:02:29,098
Type your answer.

79
00:02:30,098 --> 00:02:30,648
Press Answer.

80
00:02:31,358 --> 00:02:32,618
And the run carries on.

81
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:35,174
Spend is what it cost.

82
00:02:35,834 --> 00:02:38,434
By model, by agent type, by

83
00:02:38,434 --> 00:02:38,984
ticket.

84
00:02:39,434 --> 00:02:41,914
The scout's whole reconnaissance was three

85
00:02:41,914 --> 00:02:42,464
cents.

86
00:02:42,648 --> 00:02:44,968
Fifty five percent of those tokens

87
00:02:44,968 --> 00:02:47,148
were the manager's own context.

88
00:02:47,788 --> 00:02:49,848
Its own row, so nothing hides.

89
00:02:50,728 --> 00:02:52,028
Tyran does not know what you

90
00:02:52,028 --> 00:02:52,578
pay.

91
00:02:52,848 --> 00:02:53,988
You write the rate card.

92
00:02:54,574 --> 00:02:56,894
Two hooks will refuse things.

93
00:02:57,494 --> 00:02:59,434
A report with no command output

94
00:02:59,434 --> 00:03:00,494
is one.

95
00:03:00,794 --> 00:03:01,914
It blocks silence,

96
00:03:02,434 --> 00:03:03,014
not forgery.

97
00:03:03,421 --> 00:03:05,481
And a commit carrying a secret

98
00:03:05,481 --> 00:03:06,521
is refused.

99
00:03:07,081 --> 00:03:08,501
Even inside a markdown file.

100
00:03:09,441 --> 00:03:11,761
Install gitleaks first, or that gate

101
00:03:11,761 --> 00:03:13,021
has nothing to scan with.

102
00:03:13,607 --> 00:03:15,427
When the last ticket merges,

103
00:03:16,127 --> 00:03:17,007
try to end the session.

104
00:03:17,867 --> 00:03:18,417
It refuses.

105
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:20,017
Once.

106
00:03:20,072 --> 00:03:22,492
It reads the journals and the

107
00:03:22,492 --> 00:03:23,022
reports,

108
00:03:23,052 --> 00:03:24,872
then changes Tyran itself.

109
00:03:25,612 --> 00:03:26,492
Never your product code.

110
00:03:27,292 --> 00:03:29,632
Most retros change nothing, and that

111
00:03:29,632 --> 00:03:30,182
is correct.

112
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:33,280
The same failure three times becomes

113
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:33,880
knowledge,

114
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,380
pasted into every matching handoff.

115
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:37,820
Five times,

116
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,600
it becomes a rule in your

117
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,180
CLAUDE file.

118
00:03:40,741 --> 00:03:42,901
One line in a STOP file

119
00:03:42,901 --> 00:03:44,301
halts everything,

120
00:03:44,821 --> 00:03:45,371
from anywhere.

121
00:03:46,081 --> 00:03:47,501
You keep every decision.

122
00:03:48,261 --> 00:03:49,461
The team does the rest.
